Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: park a waiting invoke across system freeze

fastrpc_internal_invoke() sends the message and then waits with
wait_for_completion_interruptible(). When the freezer interrupts that
wait the ioctl returns -ERESTARTSYS and is restarted after thaw as a new
invoke, so the DSP receives a second copy of the still-pending call.
hexagonrpcd always keeps one listener blocked in an invoke, which is why
every system suspend produced a duplicate and the sensor DSP crashed
shortly after tasks restarted (EX:sensor_process:0x1:frpc_dsp:0x6c).

Wait with TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE instead. The freezer then
parks the sleeping caller in place; a completion that arrives while it is
parked is kept for the thaw, and a real signal still returns
-ERESTARTSYS with the existing interrupted-invoke bookkeeping. The
kernel-invoke timeout branch and the errored-context cleanup are
untouched.

Reference: omarchy-mobile f702f68 devices/oneplus7pro/kernel/sensors/
fastrpc-freezable-wait.patch.
Nura-Category: upstream-fix
Nura-Origin: omarchy-mobile f702f688 fastrpc-freezable-wait
Upstream-Status: not in mainline v7.2 (interruptible wait)
---
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -1237,7 +1237,15 @@
 		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&ctx->work, 10 * HZ))
 			err = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else {
-		err = wait_for_completion_interruptible(&ctx->work);
+		/*
+		 * Freezable, so that system suspend parks a waiting caller
+		 * instead of interrupting it. An interrupted invoke is
+		 * restarted as a second message for the same call, and the
+		 * sensor DSP crashes on it (EX:sensor_process:frpc_dsp) as
+		 * soon as tasks are thawed.
+		 */
+		err = wait_for_completion_state(&ctx->work,
+						TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE);
 	}
 
 	if (err)
